# Information about the assignment 

In this group assignment, you will **reanalyze an existing dataset** using the Bayesian graphical modeling methodology introduced in the workshop. You are provided with a short study description and a **fully specified Methods section**. Your task is to:

* Implement the analysis exactly as implied by the Methods section
* Make justified analytical decisions where choices are left open
* Write a very bried **Results section** where the results are summarized.

You will work with the **French subsample (N = 490)** from the original study, using **18 ordinal items** from the **Short Boredom Proneness Scale (SBPS)** and the **Curiosity and Exploration Inventory–II (CEI-II)**.

```{r}
#| eval: false
#| warning: false
#| include: false
data <- read_csv("N0271_1_raw data.csv")
data_filtered <- data %>%
   filter(sample == "fr") %>%
    select(starts_with("A"), starts_with("G"), starts_with("S"), starts_with("C")) %>%
    select(-SBPS_IMC_6, -CEIII_IMC7, -sample)

saveRDS(data_filtered, "data_group_assignment.rds")



# rename the second variable to Gender
colnames(data_filtered)[2] <- "Gender"

data_filtered$Gender <- as.factor(data_filtered$Gender)

summary(data_filtered)

# check if there is NAs in the data
sum(is.na(data_filtered))
```


